(1) The Executive Manager shall —
(a) take into his custody or under his control, the property (wherever situate) to which the company is or appears to be entitled;
(b) investigate the affairs, bus iness and property of the company;
(c) as soon as practicable, report to  the Minister the results of his investigation in such manner as the Minister may direct;
